<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏpīna</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπω, πέπτω</span>, to cook,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
			cook-shop</i>, <i>victualling-house</i>, <i>eating-house</i> (syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caupona, taberna): bibitur, estur, quasi in
					popinā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 4, 2, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil. 2, 28, 69</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 11,
			24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Ner. 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2, 4, 62</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id. Ep. 1, 14, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 1,
				42, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 70,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 8, 172</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 81</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the food sold at a
				cookshop</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si epulae potius quam popinae nominandae sunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 3, 8, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">taeterrimam popinam inhalare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Pis. 6, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
